; Digit-leading enum members: the WebGPU case, and PNGine's migration
; reference.
;
; `GPUTextureDimension` is spelled `"1d"`, `"2d"`, `"3d"` in the WebGPU
; spec. None of those can be written as a bare SJON symbol: the lexer sees
; a digit-leading token and reads it as a unit-bearing number (value `2`,
; unit `d`). Before SJON 1.2.0 a host had two options, both bad: ship the
; enum as numbers with a comment (`:view-dimension 3 ; cube`, one lookup
; table per author to memorise) or as strings, giving up member checking.
;
; Now a `:symbol` member-set may declare such a spelling directly. Two
; things to know about how it works:
;
;   * **`name` is the spelling, matching is on the pair.** The member is
;     named `2d` for diagnostics, exports, and completions, but the
;     validator compares the value's parsed `(magnitude, unit)` pair, so
;     `2d`, `2.0d`, and `02d` are all the same member, and `2.5d` is not
;     any of them. Text comparison could not say that, and the binary
;     walker has no source text to compare against.
;
;   * **The value stays a number.** It is *accepted* in a symbol slot, not
;     rewritten: the tree, the binary IR, and the JSON bridge all carry
;     `{"$num": [2, "d"]}`. That is why the exported JSON Schema pins
;     `$num` for these members and `$sym` for the ordinary ones, and a schema
;     claiming `{"$sym": "2d"}` would reject a document the validator
;     accepts.
;
; A mixed set is the realistic shape: `GPUTextureViewDimension` has
; digit-leading members *and* ordinary ones side by side.

(plugin :name dimensions :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name texture-dimension
    :description "GPUTextureDimension, spelled the way the WebGPU spec spells it."
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [1d 2d 3d]))

  (value-kind :name view-dimension
    :description "GPUTextureViewDimension: digit-leading and ordinary members in one set."
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set
      (member :name 1d)
      (member :name 2d
        :label "2D"
        :description "The default view dimension.")
      (member :name 2d-array
        :description "A hyphenated digit-leading spelling, one token only because a `-` may join two letter runs inside a unit.")
      (member :name cube)
      (member :name cube-array)
      (member :name 3d)))

  (form :name texture
    :description "A texture and the view it is sampled through."
    (key :name name      :type symbol)
    (key :name dimension :type texture-dimension :optional true)
    (key :name view      :type view-dimension    :optional true)))
